# Browser proving assets are runtime files, not local build output — the app
# cannot generate a proof without them, so they are tracked despite their size.
#
# Only *_final.zkey. A `*_0000.zkey` is the pre-contribution intermediate of the
# phase-2 setup (`groth16 setup` -> `zkey contribute` -> `_final`); nothing loads
# one, build_vault_v2.ps1 deletes it, and shipping ~41 MB of them alongside a
# single-party setup invites the wrong conclusion about the ceremony.
!frontend/public/circuits/
!frontend/public/circuits/*.wasm
!frontend/public/circuits/*_final.zkey
!frontend/public/circuits/v2/
!frontend/public/circuits/v2/*.wasm
!frontend/public/circuits/v2/*_final.zkey

# The committed leaf ordering. Soroban RPC retains events only ~7 days and this
# pool's deposits are already past that, so these files are the durable record
# of which commitment sits at which leaf index. Losing them makes EVERY note in
# the pool unspendable, not just a missing one. They must never be ignored.
!/deployments/testnet-vault-v2-tree.json
!/frontend/public/tree-snapshot.json

# Local archives and handover bundles. These are snapshots of the working tree,
# not sources — committing one would embed a copy of the repo inside the repo.
*.7z
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# One-off debugging scripts. `check_relayer.js` was tracked with a hardcoded
# testnet seed in it — a 14-line balance check is not worth a committed key.
# Keep throwaways like this out of the index rather than sanitising them.
/backend/check_relayer.js

# Relayer ASP leaf mirror: local service state, rebuilt per deployment.
# Not secret (leaves are public on-chain), but it must never be shared between
# stacks - a mirror from another deployment breaks every deposit.
backend/relayer/asp-leaves.json
